; OVERVIEW
; The "hidden BASIC ROM": the second half of the CS24 chip, visible at 4000H-7FFFH
; when page 1 = bank 3 and port 3DH b2 = 0.  NEXTSTMT/EVFUNC (P0-B0) enter it for
; every keyword whose token-table bank byte is 06H, through the jump table at
; 4000H-40D8H.  Contents: program-level commands (CONT, AUTO, LIST, NEW, PASS,
; TRON/TROFF, TITLE, RENUM, ON ..., KEY), clock and alarm (TIME$, DATE$, ALARM$,
; BEEP), analog input (ADIN, AIN), the serial port statements (COM, SETCOM,
; OUTSTAT, INSTAT, RCVSTAT, SNDSTAT, SNDBRK, SETDEV, PCONSOLE, PZONE, COM$, PHONE),
; files and devices (OPN, INIT, MAXFILES, OPEN, CLOSE, PRINT#, INPUT#, KILL, NAME,
; SET, FILES, LFILES, COPY, SAVE, LOAD, BSAVE, BLOAD, EOF) and the LCD graphics
; statements (PSET, PRESET, GPRINT, GCURSOR; LINE is in P1-B0 in the OLD revision).
; Handlers follow the statement convention of P0-B0 NEXTSTMT: HL = processing
; pointer, return NC = done or C with A = error code.
; ============================================================================

; ---- I/O ports ----
P_LH10:     equ 10H     ; LH-5811 compatible block 10H-1FH (base)
